course: dictionary
lesson: 11215
title: Wont: a habit, not a mistake
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old books and very formal writing. «Wont» is one of them. As a noun it means a habit, the usual way someone does things. In the phrase «be wont to» it means usually does.
explain: Look at the context: «As dawn comes, no birds sang as they were wont to do.» The birds did not sing this time, so they must have usually sung at dawn. Wont means used to. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Try «used to» in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Be careful, because wont with no apostrophe is also a common spelling mistake for won't, which means will not. Ask: does the sentence talk about a habit, or about refusing or not doing something in future? A habit means wont. Will not means won't.
fact: «Wont» means habit, or the usual way someone does things.
fact: «As is his wont» means as he usually does.
fact: «Be wont to» means usually does; it is formal and old-fashioned.
fact: In everyday speech, people say usually or as always instead of wont.
fact: Wont with no apostrophe is a common misspelling of won't, which means will not, and it is a spelling mistake in school writing.
exercise: «As dawn comes, no birds sang as they were wont to do.» What does wont mean here? | Very loudly | Forgot | Will not | *Used to
exercise: In an old story: «as was her wont, Granny took a walk after tea». What does «as was her wont» mean? | *As she usually did | As she was told to | As she never did | As she was angry
exercise: Which spelling is correct in school writing? «I ___ forget my kit again.» | wont | woant | *won't | wonts
test: «The old dog was wont to sleep by the fire.» What does wont mean? | *Habit, or what it usually did | Refused to | Very cold | Hurt badly
test: What is the best everyday way to say «as is his wont»? | As he will not do | As he has forgotten | As he was angry | *As he usually does
exam: Jay writes «I wont go to the park» in a school story. What is the mistake? | Nothing, wont is correct school spelling | *It should be won't, which means will not | It should be wont, meaning habit | It should be wonted
